<SiteLayout title="Privacy | Enterprise IT Fixes" description="Privacy information for visitors to Enterprise IT Fixes.">
  <div class="page"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Privacy'}]} /><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1 class="page-title">Privacy information</h1><p class="page-lead">This page describes the data practices of the current site implementation.</p>
    <article class="article"><h2>Data collected by this site</h2><p>The site has no account system, contact form, newsletter, comments, or database. The search feature runs in your browser and searches the guide index served with the site. It does not send search terms to a third-party search service.</p><h2>Hosting logs</h2><p>The hosting provider may process request data such as IP addresses and browser details in its server logs. Cloudflare Web Analytics is enabled for this Pages site; Cloudflare states that Web Analytics does not use cookies or collect personal data. Google Analytics is currently not active on the site.</p><h2>Google AdSense and consent</h2><p>The Google AdSense tag is loaded on site pages to connect the site to AdSense and provide its European consent message. It is not loaded on this privacy page. AdSense ad placements and Auto ads are currently disabled while Google reviews the site. If Google displays its consent message, visitors can allow, refuse, or manage the listed data uses and advertising partners. Google's services may process device or browser information for advertising and measurement as described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">Google's information for sites and apps that use its services</a>. The consent message is configured in English, Dutch, and French; Google may take time to begin displaying it after publication. Where Google provides its consent controls, visitors can use them to revisit or withdraw their choice.</p><h2>Advertising and commercial links</h2><p>No ad placements, affiliate links, or paid sponsor placements are currently active. If that changes, this notice will be updated to explain the relevant providers and data practices. Commercial recommendations will be clearly labelled.</p><h2>External links</h2><p>Guide pages and project pages can link to vendor documentation or GitHub. Those services apply their own privacy practices.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>This static site has no direct contact form. Corrections can be proposed through the linked public repository issue tracker.</p></article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
